 \paragraph{The joint cost is heterogeneous.}
 For C7, the mean interval for $L^\star-\eta$ is $[\BoundedPremiumLowerCseven,\BoundedPremiumUpperCseven]$, but its lower endpoints have median only $0.000389$ and range $[0.0000349,0.06254]$. Two conditions---Llama-3.1-8B/layer 13 and Llama-3.2-3B/layer 11---contribute $90.7\%$ of their sum. D4 has mean interval $[\BoundedPremiumLowerDfour,\BoundedPremiumUpperDfour]$, lower-endpoint median $0.01876$ and range $[0.00254,0.08719]$. All conditions retain equal weight. The mean is therefore insufficient to describe the weekday guarantees. Moreover, positivity of $p^-$ follows from $\eta>0$ under the theorem; the data inform its magnitude and distribution, not a separate positivity discovery.
 
